## Why This Is Asked

This question probes real-time risk handling, cross-functional negotiation, and release engineering under regulatory pressure.

## Key Concepts

- Incident risk assessment and decision framing
- Canary releases and feature flags
- Rollback plans and rollback testing
- Privacy, regulatory compliance, and data governance
- Stakeholder alignment and concise communication

## Code Example

```javascript
// gated rollout example
if (featureFlags.analyticsEnabled && privacy.isCompliant()) {
  enableAnalytics();
} else {
  enableFallbackAnalytics();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure success of the chosen path?
- What changes would you make to incident playbooks to cover similar risks in the future?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to surface interests, frame decisions, and balance speed with compliance in cross‑functional conflicts.

## Key Concepts

- Interest-based negotiation
- Mediation charter and grounding rules
- Trade-off analysis: speed vs risk
- Post-resolution feedback loop and learning

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: scoring options by impact on risk, speed, and cost
function scoreOption(option) {
  // option = {risk, speed, cost}
  // Higher is better
  return option.speed * 2 - option.risk * 3 - option.cost;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you ensure accountability after the decision is implemented?
- What guardrails would you put in place to prevent similar conflicts?

